Appends a method stub, and creates the import block its signature needs.

Adding a declaration is the other thing the patch language cannot express: a
patch has to match something, and a new declaration matches nothing. This also
covers the case that defeats the patch engine's `add param --import` — the file
has no imports at all, so the block has to be created rather than extended.

-- args --
add method Queue.Wait app/app.go --params "ctx context.Context" --results error --import context

-- patterns --

-- go.mod --
module example.com/typedadd

go 1.22

-- app/app.in.go --
package app

// Queue holds work.
type Queue struct {
	Depth int
}

-- app/app.out.go --
package app

import "context"

// Queue holds work.
type Queue struct {
	Depth int
}

func (r *Queue) Wait(ctx context.Context) error {
	panic("not implemented")
}
